  "decision_protocol": [
    "Verify source/worker provenance, pinned input hashes, all 555 selection rows and unchanged labels before audio.",
    "Use every 16384-sample short window on a fixed 8192-sample grid plus the last window. Measure each exactly once.",
    "At each short-window center use a clamped 65536-sample Hann spectrum, or the full shorter take. No input normalization or pitch shift.",
    "Report label-blind periodicity and strongest spectral peaks, with eight-harmonic energy bands at label, expected cents, plus/minus octave, open string, neighboring labels and periodic estimate.",
    "Compare full trajectories with same-string/same-note controls; distinguish sustained non-octave disagreement, octave ambiguity and variable/weak observations. Describe evidence without automatic truth labels.",
    "No retry, tuning, model/refit or source treatment follows automatically. Tracker acceptance remains the existing held-out, per-label and false-output gates."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This is a targeted diagnostic subset selected after the earlier result, not an unbiased performance test or a new held-out score.",
    "The short-window estimator is unchanged. Independent long-window spectra expose harmonic ambiguity; agreement does not prove the intended pitch or played string.",
    "An even-harmonics-only lower note and an upper octave can have indistinguishable waveforms. Do not infer a corrected label from that case.",
    "Spectral windows are centered retrospective observations; no causal or latency claim. Short takes use their full available length and report native frequency resolution. Zero padding only interpolates.",
    "Overlapping windows are correlated. Counts describe this take, not independent examples or unique audio duration.",
    "All selected takes, silent/unresolved windows and missing controls retained. No relabeling, exclusion, model fit, threshold sweep, score update or installed change.",
    "Metadata neighbors are labeled pitches, not verified sounding notes; selected excerpts do not include the full original performance between takes."
  ]
